A||||5||Old Lar||Hangers||||9||
Z||000000||Old Lar||09-01-2000||09:12 AM||||I had a rear exhaust pipe hanger break on my 87 GT. The bracket screws into a panel under the car and is connected to a rubber piece then a metal hook which clamps to the exhaust pipe. The hook part broke (rusted)  GM doesn't have the part..- discontinued.   Mr Goodwrench welded some pieces together for a fix.  I needed the repair.  The Borla system is only held on the pipe at the cat and the two rear hangers. The next trip to a bone yard look for the simple parts.  When I get out to Kick Hill Farms, I'll have to see if Bob has this type of part in his barn.  I was told the these hangers are different for the 87 and 88s. I'll have to look.<P>I almost thought of the coathanger fix. Naa too tacky.  Spending an afternoon under the Fiero in the driveway is not my idea of a good time.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||09-01-2000||09:32 AM||||The hanger that you speak of is in the general shape and configureation of most 'universail hangers'. all you should have to do is to cut off the excess material on the top. This type hanger can be twisted to conform to almost any configuration as they have two areas on rivets that can be turned.<BR>You may need to drill a new hole in the mounting bracket to use the factory mounting hole in the frame.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||09-01-2000||09:45 AM||||Trak Auto (and possibly others) carry a kit that has the strap and the clamp. All you need to do is remove your old one drill out the rivits on the top bracket and use bolts to attach the new assembly. You can even clean off the top part and paint it to prevent any future rust. They are $12.99 for the kit (need one per side)<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||09-01-2000||12:35 PM||||Thanks for the leads.  I may check out some parts places to see if the generic hanger will fit.  I'll crawl back under to check the other side.  90 degrees this weekend and me on my back on a blacktopped driveway. What fun.<P>I want it back together for next weekend I'm going to try to get to a Canadian show up near Toronto.  I'll miss the NIFE show, but Fierobob, was talking of trailering my 88 to the NIFE show if it gets all together.<P>I'm putting together the woodgrain dash kit from GTracer tonight, to ship back to Bob for install.  I did the radio/guage pod last night.  It seems like a one shot try, the veneer sticks real quick, no time for a missed alignment.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodney||09-02-2000||07:33 PM||||I am looking to replicate all the hangers. It will mean several pieces will need to be laser cut. I am also having a hard time finding good clamps. GM and the rest use them by the millions. I wish I could find their suppliers. I'd like to find the 409 stainless steel ones. I'll probably end up using 304 stainless steel ones.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gokart||09-02-2000||08:13 PM||||I'm all for the stainless steel clamps Rodney! My exhaust system was only a year old when I bought a set of original stainless steel tips and the clamps were so rusted one broke trying to get it off <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> Let us know when you've completed the project <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||14
